<h1 class="mt-3">About Local Connect</h1>
<p class="text-muted" style="font-size:14px;">Connecting communities across Nepal</p>

<p>Local Connect is a hyperlocal community platform built to bridge the gap between citizens, verified organizations,
    and community administrators in Nepal.</p>

<p>The platform enables trusted, location-based communication — so residents always know what's happening in their area,
    and organizations can reach the people who matter most.</p>

<h2>What we support</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Alerts</strong> — urgent local notices like road closures, outages, safety warnings, and weather events
    </li>
    <li><strong>Events</strong> — community gatherings, programs, and local activities</li>
    <li><strong>Volunteer Opportunities</strong> — organizations post drives and citizens can sign up directly</li>
    <li><strong>Notices & Training</strong> — official announcements and skill-building programs</li>
    <li><strong>Community Updates</strong> — regular updates from verified community pages</li>
</ul>

<h2>Who uses Local Connect</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Citizens</strong> — residents who want to stay informed and participate in their community</li>
    <li><strong>Organizations</strong> — verified NGOs, businesses, and institutions that serve the public</li>
    <li><strong>Community Admins</strong> — approved local representatives managing a specific area page</li>
</ul>

<h2>Our mission</h2>
<p>To make local information accessible, trustworthy, and actionable — so every community member can stay connected,
    contribute, and respond when it matters.</p>